(Reflection Notes: DGU IndustryBridge is a project-based student–business platform designed to connect local) Tj
T* (businesses with relevant DGU student teams for clearly defined, short-term business projects. Through the) Tj
T* (Venture Quest process, I have identified the core customer problem, defined the initial beachhead segment,) Tj
T* (developed the value proposition, considered existing alternatives, designed a revenue model, estimated the initial) Tj
T* (market opportunity, and created a practical go-to-market and MVP plan.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (However, several important assumptions are still unvalidated. The most critical assumption is that small and) Tj
T* (medium-sized businesses in Selaqui and nearby Dehradun have suitable short-term problems and are willing to) Tj
T* (pay for solutions delivered by DGU student teams. I also need to validate whether businesses trust students with) Tj
T* (real projects and whether student teams can consistently deliver useful outputs within the agreed scope and) Tj
T* (timeline.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The next step is therefore not to build a full application, but to run a 30-day validation experiment. I will approach at) Tj
T* (least 15–20 local businesses through direct outreach, DGU faculty/alumni referrals, LinkedIn and local business) Tj
T* (networks. I will conduct customer interviews to identify actual business problems and understand current) Tj
T* (alternatives. From the qualified prospects, I will propose small pilot projects with clearly defined scope, timelines,) Tj
T* (deliverables and pricing.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The initial target is to secure at least 2 paid pilot projects, complete them with suitable DGU student teams, collect) Tj
T* (structured customer feedback and measure willingness to recommend or repeat the service. I will use the results) Tj
T* (to determine whether the problem, customer segment, pricing and student-delivery model need to be refined) Tj
T* (before investing in a dedicated digital platform.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The key learning from this venture exercise is that the idea should be treated as a set of testable assumptions) Tj
T* (rather than as a proven business model. The immediate goal is to generate real evidence from businesses and) Tj
T* (completed projects. If the evidence supports the assumptions, I can gradually expand the service and develop) Tj
T* (technology around the validated workflow. If the evidence disproves an important assumption, I will modify the) Tj
T* (customer segment, project categories, pricing or business model before scaling.) Tj
